    "biography": "William Nickerson was an English settler who became the founder of Chatham, Massachusetts in the mid-17th century. Originally a weaver by trade from Norwich, England, he immigrated to the American colonies in 1637 with his wife Anne Busby and four children, initially settling in Salem before moving to Cape Cod. Nickerson was a pioneering land surveyor who made significant early land purchases from the local Native American Monomoyick tribe, specifically from Sachem Mattaquason, which enabled the establishment of the settlement that would become Chatham. He is considered a key early colonial settler who took substantial personal and economic risks in establishing a new community in the Massachusetts Bay Colony.",
